aid so let's set the  record straight chris hemsworth wants to  continue to play thor he wants to  continue to be a part of the marvel  cinematic universe and i think a lot of  other people want him to stay in the mcu  as well especially since we don't really  have that many original avengers left  and who knows when the other ones are  going to be leaving now there could  actually be even more thor's joining the  mcu than just jane foster's thor and  chris hemsworth's thor which is a really  cool thought and this also kind of leans  more towards the fact that we'll see  chris hemsworth's thor again because  check out what marvel studios president  kevin feige had to say about the future  of the thor franchise in an interview  with slash film in this interview  discussion came around to the future of  the thor franchise and the possibility  of other thor's beyond jane and chris  hemsworth's character entering the mcu  in which kevin feige said there are  these things called comic books that  have a lot of stories in them and that's  where all of our stories come from and  if the question is have you told all of  the great horror stories from the comics  and movies the answer is no there are  lots of them and i've always said our  interest in making additional stories is  somewhat about continuing the character  it's almost entirely about continuing  the experience with the actor and being  able to see i think of all of our casts  not as their individual characters but  as the marvel players who within that  character can grow and evolve and change  and if we look at the comics as our  guide there are plenty of other  incarnations of thor that we have yet to  see now this is fantastic news for chris  hemsworth staying in the mcu but right  away what i actually think about when i  hear kevin feige say this or read what  he said is i automatically think of beta  ray bill when we think of other  incarnations of thor this is exactly  what i think of in my head in for  ra